WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.350
Did you know that the blue tassels that are
hanging out from the sides of Buggy´s hat

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:07.629
are actually his hair tied together in two
ponytails?

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:09.310
There you go.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:13.780
Even if you decide to stop watching this video
right now, I hope that this at least blew

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.300
your mind a little.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.330
I´ve talked a lot about One Piece and have
analyzed a lot of characters.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.270
But one thing that I never would have guessed
would be so interesting to discuss within

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.580
this series in particular is Buggy.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:32.020
When you guys rose to my challenge last week
and chose him for the next video, I didn´t

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.530
expect Buggy to be able to teach us as much
about One Piece, as it turns out that he actually

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:37.670
does.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:43.380
Not only is Buggy a perfect representation
of the story One Piece itself, but he also

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.570
teaches us a lot about what the actual One
Piece might be.

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:51.660
And speaking of the challenge, you guys did
an amazing Job.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:55.859
What better time to take a closer look at
the warlords, then right now, where they might

00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:58.550
become super relevant to the story again?

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:04.129
Also, since last week´s challenge was a crushing
defeat for me, since you managed to get 2000

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:09.090
likes in just 7 HOURS, I think we have to
raise the bar a little for the next one and

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:11.000
see if you can still make it.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:17.050
So, if you manage to bring this video to 3000
likes in the first 24 hours, the next warlord

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.140
video will be out by next Tuesday.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:25.590
But now, grab yourself a big cup of your favorite
hot or cold beverage of choice, we have to

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:29.100
talk about Buggy.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.439
Buggy the Clown has earned his epithet for
a reason.

00:01:32.439 --> 00:01:37.299
His character design is centered around the
varying theme of a circus clown mixed with

00:01:37.299 --> 00:01:39.310
that of a pirate.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:43.729
Most of the time we can see Buggy wearing
makeup as well as his quite clowny white gloves

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:45.340
and pointy shoes.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:50.430
The rest of his outfit is that of a pirate
admiral with a big marine-like coat and a

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.500
pirate hat.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.659
If you ask yourself why anyone would freely
choose to dress in that way, the answer to

00:01:56.659 --> 00:01:59.719
that is Buggy´s most prominent clown feature.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:01.979
His big red nose.

00:02:01.979 --> 00:02:07.829
Because this nose is not just another part
of his costume, but his real, actual nose.

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:12.340
It doesn´t come as a big surprise then that
Buggy has always been very sensitive about

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:18.360
this and most likely is the main reason for
his insecurity that drives his character.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:24.080
This goes so far that Buggy at one point even
destroys an entire town, when kids make fun

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.080
of his nose.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:30.750
BUT, he has made the most of his unique looks
and embraced the, at first look a little quirky

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.280
looking clown theme.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:37.220
However, if we are all completely honest,
I think we can all admit that Buggy´s design

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.160
is actually pretty cool.

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:44.480
And if One Piece teaches us one thing, it´s
that whether someone looks weird or badass

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:49.490
is mostly determined by that character’s
personality and strength.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:53.030
While he was actually introduced as a quite
shallow villain very early on in the story

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:58.950
by Oda, his popularity with the fans and Oda
himself lead to Buggy slowly but steadily

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.620
getting a more and more refined character
built.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:06.670
So much so that his backstory is as far from
shallow as it gets.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:11.480
Born somewhere on the Grand line, Buggy served
as an apprentice on the ship of the pirate

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.480
king himself.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:18.050
While at first it appears as if he didn´t
enjoy his time there at all, we slowly but

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:24.590
steadily learn that he had a much closer relationship
to his crew than we all initially thought.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:29.430
We now know, that during his time on the Oro
Jackson, he highly respects and admires Rayleigh

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:30.700
and Oden.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:35.810
And just like Shanks, Buggy must have had
a very close relationship with Roger, since

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.120
we can see him crying at his captain´s execution.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:43.930
And speaking of Shanks, while at first it
seemed like Buggy detested his fellow apprentice,

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:48.630
it more and more looks like they actually
also had a quite close relationship.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:53.230
Not only do the Marines describe their relationship
as a 'brotherly bond', but even Whitebeard

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:57.070
states that he remembers the two always being
together.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:01.480
Seeing the two arm in arm on board of the
Oro Jackson really rounds this impression

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:02.510
off.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:07.090
And as we know, Shanks even invited buggy
to join him after Roger´s death.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:11.790
Buggy however decided to leave the world of
the Yonko´s and Pirate King´s behind and

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.200
tries to make a name for himself, outside
of the New World.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:20.820
So, despite his quite exciting and unexpected
backstory, we first meet Buggy in the East

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:25.650
Blue in Orange Town as one of the first major
antagonists of the crew.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:31.960
But what really is it about the clown that
makes him into such a fan favorite?

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:36.620
While the initial impression with Buggy is
often that he is a weak and incapable pirate,

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.670
that is actually not the case.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.680
On the contrary, Buggy is quite smart.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:46.760
He has an eye for opportunities and understands
to influence and deceive those around him.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:51.630
A good example for this is Buggy recruiting
dozens of strong prisoners from Impel Down

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:55.030
into his crew and joining the ranks of the
Shijibukai.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:59.050
All after having to join Luffy on his way
into the depth of the prison and onto the

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:00.970
battlefield at Marineford.

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:07.070
Plus, we know that he is a very capable chemist,
developing his own variety of weapons, like

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:08.610
the Buggy Balls.

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:12.980
And while Buggy certainly is not comparable
to other members of the Roger pirates in terms

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:16.560
of fighting strength, he is by no means weak.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.860
Having fought alongside and against many legendary
pirates, even if a bit reluctantly, surely

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.120
has left its mark on him.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:29.610
Also, Buggy wields a quite formidable devil
fruit power, that not only allows him to float,

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:33.120
but also avoid attacks of the likes of Zoro
and Mihawk.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:39.340
A defining trait of Buggy, that he partly
shares with Luffy, is his dumb luck.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:43.889
No matter how dire the situation looks, Buggy
always manages to pull his head out of the

00:05:43.889 --> 00:05:45.370
sling somehow.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:50.110
No matter if it´s escaping Smoker, being
struck by lightning, being slashed by Mihawk

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:52.840
or even be frozen by Aokiji.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:58.680
Buggy somehow always makes it out of these
situations alive and sometimes even for the

00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.680
better.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:03.520
The truly charming part about his personality,
however, is the weird mix between comic relief

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:06.710
and serious character that he brings to the
story.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:11.460
His purpose in the story seems to alternate
between simply making the reader laugh or

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:15.110
actually impacting the plot in meaningful
ways.

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:21.139
On the one hand, Buggy is often very hysterical
and tends to cause confusion by misunderstanding

00:06:21.139 --> 00:06:24.230
or miscommunicating when talking to others.

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:29.419
On the other hand, however, we know of Buggy´s
insecurities and how he has to overcome them

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:32.330
in order to become a better person.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:37.760
Slowly he has become more and more relevant
to the actual plot of the story.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:42.310
This weird mix has led to Buggy getting a
quite significant amount of character development

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:46.110
over the course of the story, despite his
initial design.

00:06:46.110 --> 00:06:51.020
In a way, I think you could argue that it´s
the same recipe that Oda has used with Shanks.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:55.640
A character that was introduced as a simple
and comic character at the beginning of the

00:06:55.640 --> 00:07:00.250
story that slowly turned out to be more and
more of a big deal.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.960
A really big piece of evidence that Buggy
is an important character to Oda, is that

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.800
he has a dream.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:10.020
Buggy also wants to become the Pirate King.

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:14.310
And once again Oda takes a twist on that dream
with his character.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:18.639
While for Luffy, the Pirate King is the person
with the most freedom, and for Blackbeard

00:07:18.639 --> 00:07:24.070
the one with the most power, for Buggy the
Pirate King is the one with the most fortune

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.650
in the world.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:28.680
He thinks of treasure in terms of gold and
silver.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:32.550
But nonetheless, he also has a dream that
he strives to fulfill.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:37.620
So, if you ever wondered, why Buggy is such
a popular, character, it’s because he has

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:41.430
gained a lot more depth over the course of
the story, than we all could have anticipated,

00:07:41.430 --> 00:07:45.729
when we first got to meet him.

00:07:45.729 --> 00:07:51.111
Now, what does all of this have to do with
One Piece and more importantly with THE One

00:07:51.111 --> 00:07:52.510
Piece.

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:55.840
Well that´s where we have to look at Buggy´s
character Arc.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:01.130
You see Buggy´s arc over the course of the
story can be summarized as a sort of personification

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:02.460
of the story.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:07.410
When we meet him in the East Blue in Orange
Town he is the first major antagonist to Luffy,

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:08.410
Zoro and Nami.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:14.120
He starts out as a quite stereotypical, predictable
and purely comic villain that our heroes have

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.479
to take down.

00:08:15.479 --> 00:08:20.150
But then, just like the story itself, Buggy
starts to become a bit more serious.

00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:24.231
He gets new and new layers of background and
personality.

00:08:24.231 --> 00:08:29.950
Bit by bit he turns more and more complex
and slowly starts to get a political gravity

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:31.520
as well when becoming a warlord.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:36.009
I think you agree with me when I say that
this is exactly what happened to the story

00:08:36.009 --> 00:08:38.389
of One Piece as a whole.

00:08:38.389 --> 00:08:43.159
Starting of as a pure adventure in a world
of tropical islands and treasures, and of

00:08:43.159 --> 00:08:44.430
friends and villains.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:50.529
One Piece soon got a more heavy tone and Oda
gave his story more and more depth, character

00:08:50.529 --> 00:08:52.040
and complexity.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:57.639
Both Buggy AND the story are heavily influenced
by the main character, Monkey D. Luffy.

00:08:57.639 --> 00:09:02.949
And for both, Marineford was a central turning
point for the reader´s perception of them.

00:09:02.949 --> 00:09:06.860
During the Orange Town arc, Buggy turns a
little bit kinder after being defeated by

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:07.860
Luffy.

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:13.079
But the paramount war is the arc Buggy truly
changed the most as a character.

00:09:13.079 --> 00:09:18.790
Not only does he end up helping Luffy multiple
times, even if it initially is out of self-interest,

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:21.350
but he also grows as a pirate.

00:09:21.350 --> 00:09:26.300
Rising into the ranks of the warlords, Buggy
went from a completely comic character to

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:30.889
a tactician that has united countless strong
pirates under his banner.

00:09:30.889 --> 00:09:36.040
And even people, like Mr. 3, who are aware
of the façade he is putting on, still decide

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:37.329
to stick with him.

00:09:37.329 --> 00:09:41.160
Do you see how drastically different that
is from early Buggy?

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:44.309
He truly embodies the development of One Piece.

00:09:44.309 --> 00:09:46.879
BUT, we´re not done yet.

00:09:46.879 --> 00:09:51.870
Because Buggy not only teaches us a lot about
the story of One Piece, but also about the

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:53.290
One Piece itself.

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:57.790
The treasure left by Gol D. Roger and the
reason for the great pirate era.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:03.009
You see, despite serving under Roger himself
and wanting to become the pirate king, Buggy

00:10:03.009 --> 00:10:07.180
has no interest whatsoever in finding Raftel
and the One Piece.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:08.980
Why is that?

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:13.750
I think what this clearly tells us, is that
Buggy has at least a good idea, what the One

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:14.959
Piece is all about.

00:10:14.959 --> 00:10:18.590
And even though there is nothing he loves
more than finding treasure, he doesn´t want

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.060
anything to do with it?

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:24.939
I think the clear explanation for that, is
that the One Piece, at its core has nothing

00:10:24.939 --> 00:10:26.910
to do with gold or silver.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:30.570
Is it possible that there are some piles of
jewelry horded on Raftel?

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:31.570
Sure.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:36.420
But Buggy seems to know that the true value
of the One Piece lies with something else.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:41.839
Something, that carries such heavy implications
and consequences, that any sort of material

00:10:41.839 --> 00:10:44.480
add-ons would lose their meaning.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:49.019
As Whitebeard stated, finding the One Piece
will “shake the world to its core”.

00:10:49.019 --> 00:10:54.509
And while Buggy has developed as a character,
taking on the consequences of discovering

00:10:54.509 --> 00:10:58.829
Roger´s treasure is something that only very
few people could do.

00:10:58.829 --> 00:11:03.369
After all, Buggy shows us really well, what
treasure means to other people.

00:11:03.369 --> 00:11:07.260
He talks about this with Shanks on board of
the Oro Jackson.

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:09.829
For Buggy it means gold and silver.

00:11:09.829 --> 00:11:13.120
But for Shanks it means something than that.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:18.379
Similar like to Roger the One Piece will be
something with a unique meaning for him and

00:11:18.379 --> 00:11:21.309
like his straw hat has to Luffy.

00:11:21.309 --> 00:11:23.179
So, there you have it.

00:11:23.179 --> 00:11:26.240
Buggy actually teaches us a lot about One
Piece.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:30.110
And I think the way things are going at the
moment, we can say for certain that he will

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:32.569
become relevant to the story again soon.

00:11:32.569 --> 00:11:35.300
